#usda 1.0
(
    defaultPrim = "RoverSolar"
    upAxis = "Y"
    metersPerUnit = 1
)

# ── Rover variant: SOLAR ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# A PROFILE, in the same sense as `rover_easy` / `rover_medium` / `rover_awful`:
# it references the shared rocker-bogie base and does nothing but SELECT the
# base's own variants. It adds no prim, overrides no attribute.
#
#     power      = "battery"     finite bus, so a source has somewhere to push
#     generation = "solar"       the base's panel + its electrical membership
#
# WHY IT EXISTS. `generation = "solar"` was only ever selected AT A SCENE, one
# reference arc from the base. A profile puts a SECOND arc in front of it —
# scene → profile → base — which is how every purchasable rover configuration is
# authored (a wrapper asset the scene references), and nothing tested that the
# solar variant survives it. `scenes/tests/solar_domain_nested_ref.usda` runs
# this profile and a one-arc rover side by side; if the two disagree, the arc
# count is the only difference between them.
#
# The variant carries `prepend rel collection:components:includes =
# [</RockerBogie/SolarPanel>]` — an ABSOLUTE path, authored inside a variant, in
# the asset that owns the collection. Every reference arc must remap it. That is
# the composition this profile exercises.
def Xform "RoverSolar" (
    doc = "Solar rover profile — the rocker-bogie base with a battery bus and the solar generation variant selected, one reference arc above the base."
    prepend apiSchemas = ["LunCoCatalogAPI"]
    prepend references = @lunco://vessels/rovers/rocker_bogie.usda@</RockerBogie>
    variants = {
        string power = "battery"
        string generation = "solar"
    }
)
{
    uniform bool lunco:spawnable = true

    # Livery only — amber hull, so a solar rover is identifiable next to the
    # three handling tiers. Nothing electrical is authored here on purpose: this
    # profile must be a pure variant selection, or a passing test would only
    # prove that the profile RE-AUTHORED what the base already said.
    over "Body"
    {
        color3f[] primvars:displayColor = [(0.85, 0.62, 0.15)]
    }
}
